 ### Knot insertion root finding
-A root finding algorithm based on knot insertion with linear convergence speed and linear complexity per step [S1]. It requires index operations and memory usage grows with every iteration step, limiting the maximum number of iterations [S1]. For degree 9 (tri-cubic), it has a relative execution time of 1.0, MSE of 0.034, and max error of 0.85, making it more than 10 times slower than de Casteljau-based root finding [S1].
